# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# FIX 13 (mtk-ims-fixes kit) - crash_dump unwinder for MTK memfd maps
#
# Since the A17 sepolicy refresh, EVERY app-uid native crash produced
#   crash_dump failed to dump process <pid>:
#     Failed to initialize unwinder object: Failed to parse maps
# and /data/tombstones stayed empty (while system_server dumped fine).
#
# Root cause (audit 2026-10-21, xaga): MTK's app processes map a
# device-only named memfd  "/memfd:mf:/proc/<pid>/smaps (deleted)"
# (MTK mf: memory-service mirror). The kernel labels these inodes
# u:object_r:tmpfs:s0. libunwindstack opens every mapped file to read
# ELF build-ids; the { read getattr } denial makes parse_maps abort.
# system_server has no such mapping -> it was the only dumper that
# worked. Also granted: crash_dump enum of task siblings under
# cgroup2 (reads cgroup.procs to expand threads).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

allow crash_dump tmpfs:file { read getattr open };
allow crash_dump cgroup_v2:file { read getattr open };
